<article class="env-lemma" id="0645">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0645">Lemma <span data-tag="0645">13.19.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $K^\bullet $ be a complex of $\mathcal{A}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $K^\bullet $ has a projective resolution then $H^ n(K^\bullet ) = 0$ for $n \gg 0$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $H^ n(K^\bullet ) = 0$ for $n \gg 0$ then there exists a quasi-isomorphism $L^\bullet \to K^\bullet $ with $L^\bullet $ bounded above. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Dual to Lemma <a href="/tag/013J" data-tag="013J">13.18.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>